// CONFORMANCE-CASE
// spec: 07-resource-authority
// facility: rule.value-object.write [Write-Resource-Overwrite-Rejected]; D-0095; conf.overwrite-field-of-live-object
// kind: negative
// expect: diag.overwrite-of-live-resource (static)
//
// A field of a valid, initialized object always holds its value (moving
// one out is rejected, and a trusted raw move-out may not take cells a
// live object claims), and every value of `Tok` owns a resource: the
// assignment would lose the old `Tok`, refuted before the program
// runs. The repair is `overwrite(&mut g.start, …)`. (A `String` field
// would be replaced: `String` is quiet, D-0194.)

import std;

resource struct Tok
{
    i32 v;
}

struct Grammar
{
    Tok start;
}

fn main()
{
    Grammar g = Grammar { .start = Tok { .v = 0 } };
    g.start = Tok { .v = 1 };
}
